      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for the tip about Benford's Law, I'll definitely look into that. \n\nThe main issue is that even when I look closely at the physical receipts, they seem almost... elusive? Like, they are there, but they don't quite add up to anything meaningful, and they always seem to pop up in these tiny, nagging increments that are just enough to be annoying but not enough to be a \"crime.\" It feels like I'm chasing something that is intentionally trying to hide in the shadows of the ledger. \n\nDo you have any advice on how to deal with these kinds of \"nuisance\" anomalies that seem to evade standard detection?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
